            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, petitioner conceded that Brecht does not always subsume AEDPA, narrowing the dispute."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ff6497611b8ce1f329f9edd111da0cc34d72a95879a8a20a6a711bac81ddbe92",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ff6497611b8c-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Gorsuch, the Court\u2019s principal legal question was whether a federal court may grant habeas relief based solely on the Brecht test or must also evaluate the state court\u2019s decision under AEDPA."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Background and Question",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "case_id": "2021-20-826",
  "decision": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ff6497611b8ce1f329f9edd111da0cc34d72a95879a8a20a6a711bac81ddbe92",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ff6497611b8c-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The majority held that, under \u00a7\u202f2254(d), a federal court shall not grant habeas relief unless the statutory conditions are satisfied."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ff6497611b8ce1f329f9edd111da0cc34d72a95879a8a20a6a711bac81ddbe92",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ff6497611b8c-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The majority concluded that a proper Brecht analysis precludes relief and reversed the Ninth Circuit\u2019s ruling."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ff6497611b8ce1f329f9edd111da0cc34d72a95879a8a20a6a711bac81ddbe92",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ff6497611b8c-0003-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "ff6497611b8ce1f329f9edd111da0cc34d72a95879a8a20a6a711bac81ddbe92",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ff6497611b8c-0004-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 42,
              "start": 42
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kagan, in dissent, argued that the majority departs from precedent and forces habeas courts to \u201cspin their wheels.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ff6497611b8ce1f329f9edd111da0cc34d72a95879a8a20a6a711bac81ddbe92",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ff6497611b8c-0003-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 36,
              "start": 36
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, in dissent, Justice Kagan questioned what standard a habeas court should use to decide whether a state trial court\u2019s constitutional error was harmless."
      }
    ],
