            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Supreme Court granted certiorari to resolve a circuit conflict about the proper interaction between the Brecht test and the Antiterrorism and Effective Death Penalty Act (AEDPA)."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ff6497611b8ce1f329f9edd111da0cc34d72a95879a8a20a6a711bac81ddbe92",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ff6497611b8c-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that, under 28\u202fU.S.C.\u202f\u00a7\u202f2254(d), a federal court shall not grant habeas relief unless specific statutory conditions are satisfied."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ff6497611b8ce1f329f9edd111da0cc34d72a95879a8a20a6a711bac81ddbe92",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ff6497611b8c-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Applying a proper Brecht analysis, the Court concluded that relief was not warranted and reversed the Ninth Circuit\u2019s decision."
      }
    ],
